  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $\\int \\frac{d x}{\\sin x+\\sqrt{3} \\cos x}=\\int \\frac{d x}{2\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\sin x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cos x\\right)}=\\frac{1}{2} \\int \\frac{d x}{\\sin \\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\frac{1}{2} \\int \\operatorname{cosec}\\left(\\mathrm{x}+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\mathrm{dx}=\\frac{1}{2} \\log \\left|\\tan \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right|+\\mathrm{c} \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{2} \\ln \\left|\\tan \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right|+\\mathrm{c}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
